hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"84","Allahumma inni as'aluka al-'afwa wal-'afiyata fid-dunya wal-aakhirah. Allahumma inni as'aluka al-'afwa wal-'afiyati fi deeni wa dunyaaya wa ahli wa maali. Allahummas-tur 'awraati wa aaamin raw'aati. Allahummahfazni min bayni yadayya wa min khalfi wa 'an yameeni wa 'an shimaali, wa min fawqi, wa a'udhu bi 'azamatika an ugh-taala min tahti.. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my worldly affairs, my family, and my wealth. O Allah, conceal my faults and calm my fears. O Allah, protect me from my front, from behind me, from my right, from my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being seized from beneath me."
"85","Allāhumma ‘ālima al-ghaybi wash-shahādah, fāṭir as-samāwāti wal-arḍ, rabbi kulli shay’in wa malīkih, ashadu an lā ilāha illā anta, a‘ūdhu bika min sharri nafsī wa min sharri ash-shayṭāni wa shirkih, wa an aqtarifa ‘alā nafsī sū’an aw ajjurrahu ilā muslim.. O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Sovereign of everything, I bear witness that there is no deity except You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own soul, from the evil of Satan and his polytheism, and from committing any evil against myself or bringing it upon a Muslim."
